= Why this computes the accepted adjoint
The accepted global forward factorization is4Psi=K1 alpha H0,where
H_i are the pair of degree4 norms and K_i their Picard adjoints. Taking
adjoints gives4PsiHat=K0 alphaHat H1. The elliptic rational groups have
orders109 and113,with4 times82=1mod109 and4 times85=1mod113. The
destination Jacobian rational group has odd order12,317,so multiplication
by4 is injective there. The displayed rational-point algorithm therefore
computes the old PsiHat. It supplies no global inverse morphism of[4].
PRIME_FIELD_ADJOINT.md retains upstream526f9f/4934b4/78176c and the old
quotient,Picard,polarization and norm dependencies. [pcc:unverified]

For a finite elliptic point P=(X,Y),the pullback uses the whole fibre
U=N-XQ² and V=YQ³/M moduloU. On this finite algebra the cover/target
identities giveF M²=Y²Q⁶,so Q and M are units even for repeated support.
The finite fibre and actual infinity multiplicities enter the unchanged
balanced reduction. The odd rational elliptic groups exclude nonzero
two-torsion;its geometric chart remains outside this implemented domain.
The original finite-algebra proof and bound QuarticFibre helpers remain
